{"kind":"report","text":"Early shared-byte-layer static review at I1 c05e89cfd1d6332fce6f607df09087b3f1c50e77, under checker request b5955cb25eef9ae70f12e73650e5cf46b49cdde0 and promise 1514419c6ed14e42689559cb7cd9449797d54592.\n\nNo additional material supported-form defect established in this bounded review. This is a source assessment, not final I1 approval or measured cryptographic/cross-runtime evidence.\n\nComplete coverage: all 15 files in packages/bytes at the frozen head. This includes all seven production/declaration files canonical.ts (239 LF), domains.ts (91), encode.ts (75), hash.ts (23), index.ts (5), sign.ts (44), web.d.ts (14); README, manifest, both tsconfigs and vitest config; both complete tests and the complete fixed fixture. Numbered production/config/doc reading totals 26263 characters; both tests/fixture were read through EOF. Pertinent adopted R1 v7:67–160 byte-domain/identity clauses were reread, and current validator:71–225 and judgeAct:68–108 were reread to distinguish primitive encoding from admission. Full earlier I1 contract-delta reading transfers at this immutable head.\n\nSource observations: all six wrappers use the contract's tag plus one newline and canonical bytes; intent digest excludes its signature, entry hash is built beside the entry, scope identity derives from the seed domain, and incarnation encoding requires exactly 16 caller-supplied bytes. The canonical writer/parser consistently bound nesting at 64, reject unsafe/non-integer/negative-zero forms and lone surrogates, detect decoded duplicate keys, preserve __proto__ as an ordinary own property, and reject malformed UTF-8/BOM. Encodings reject impossible lengths and set trailing bits rather than admitting multiple text forms. Ed25519 checking delegates to the pinned synchronous library with zip215 false; verifySignedIntent catches malformed input. The Web API declarations and common-library configs explicitly state the primitive runtime dependencies. These are properties